    "tool_calls": 30,
    "summary": "Fixed the wfmt container implementation against the authoritative samples.\n\nKey findings from assets/sample.wfmt (specification-by-example):\n- Header: b\"WFMT\", version 1, big-endian u32 record count (as in the draft).\n- Records: tag uvarint, payload-length uvarint, payload; no alignment padding.\n- Trailer: 4-byte little-endian CRC-32 of everything before it, using the standard zlib/bzip2 CRC-32 (final XOR with 0xFFFFFFFF — the draft's \"no final XOR\" was the bug).\n\nFixes:\n- crc.py: compute_crc now applies the final XOR, making it equivalent to zlib.crc32 (matches both samples, including sample_empty). unpack_crc raises WFormatError(\"truncated\") instead of ValueError.\n- varint.py: decode_uvarint implemented as a real multi-byte LEB128 decoder (>10 bytes → kind \"varint\"; insufficient data → kind \"truncated\").\n- codec.py: unpack now validates the trailer checksum and raises WFormatError(kind=\"checksum\") on mismatch; truncation inside records is re-classified properly; short-container pre-c",
    "changed_workspace": true
  },
